  "locked": false,
  "title": "fix(short_qa): keep the SPECS line for videos without an audio stream",
  "user": {
    "login": "crenamu",
    "id": 41649816,
    "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQxNjQ5ODE2",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41649816?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/crenamu",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/crenamu",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/crenamu/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/crenamu/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/crenamu/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/crenamu/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/crenamu/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/crenamu/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/crenamu/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/crenamu/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/crenamu/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "A render without an audio stream loses the first line of `report.md`.\n\n```python\nR.append(f\"SPECS ... s; audio: \"\n         + \", \".join(f\"{s['codec_name']} ...\" for s in au) if au else \"NONE\")\n```\n\nThe conditional is attached to the whole `R.append(...)` argument, so when `au` is empty the script appends the bare string `\"NONE\"` instead of the SPECS line. Width, height, fps, frame count and duration then never reach the report - the numbers you need most when triaging a render that came out silent.\n\n### Reproduce\n\n```bash\nffmpeg -f lavfi -i \"testsrc2=size=1080x1920:rate=30\" -t 2 -pix_fmt yuv420p silent.mp4\npython templates/scripts/short_qa.py silent.mp4 out\nhead -1 out/report.md\n```\n\nBefore:\n\n```\nNONE\n```\n\nAfter:\n\n```\nSPECS 1080x1920 30/1 fps, 60 frames, 2.000 s; audio: NONE\n```\n\n### Fix\n\nBuild the audio description first, then always append a complete SPECS line:\n\n```python\nau_desc = \", \".join(f\"{s['codec_name']} {s['sample_rate']} Hz {s['channels']}ch\" for s in au) or \"NONE\"\nR.append(f\"SPECS {v['width']}x{v['height']} {v['r_frame_rate']} fps, {v.get('nb_frames')} frames, \"\n         f\"{float(pr['format']['duration']):.3f} s; audio: {au_desc}\")\n```\n\nNo duplicated f-string, 3 lines changed.\n\n### Verification\n\n- Silent 1080x1920 clip: line 1 is now the full SPECS line with `audio: NONE`\n- The same clip with an AAC track: the complete `report.md` is **identical** to the current script's output (diffed line by line)\n- Nothing else touched: black/white/frozen/pop detection, per-shot stats, contact sheets and `perframe.npz` are unchanged\n",
